.SH NAME
gmb-doc-review-record-revert - Record a human revert of machine text as an observed review item


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgmb doc review record-revert [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Logs a human revert of machine-generated text as a terminal
informational observation (Kind "revert", Status "observed"). The doc and
section flags are optional; the reason is required and feeds prompt/style
tuning via 'gmb doc review --tuning'.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--doc\fP=""
	Reverted document path (optional)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for record-revert

.PP
\fB--reason\fP=""
	Why the text was reverted (required)

.PP
\fB--section\fP=""
	Reverted section ID (optional)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	Color output mode: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	Config file path (default is $HOME/.glassmarble.yaml)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--dir\fP=""
	Target repository directory for analysis and queries

.PP
\fB--max-json-mb\fP=0
	Refuse to load or commit an AKG state file (akg.json) larger than this many MiB (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Verbose output logging


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gmb doc review record-revert --doc docs/auth.md --section intro --reason "human rewrote the table"
.EE


